From c854c839c9995e726a603b027aad5bfda66c116c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allcodernet <67543055+allcodernet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 08:19:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 34/45] decide: coverage clamp, cache trim before copy, one
 cell formula, info slots

- A coverage in (1, 1 + 1e-6] (float log-probs) is reported as exactly 1,
  in score_field_full and in the debias mean; larger values stay.
- plan_cache_store decides before a snapshot is copied whether it is
  stored and which entries go; the victims are erased first, then the
  snapshot is copied. When it would not be stored nothing is erased and
  nothing is copied off the GPU; a failed copy stores nothing.
- need_for in run_request calls state_cells with the round's sums.
- /v1/decide/info also lists a slot whose seq_pos_min >= 0 (cells in
  one part of hybrid memory).
